[E0323] Error: a `for` over an iterator moves it on, and this cannot change
    ╭─[ err/169_iterators/main.wip:15:14 ]
    │
 15 │     for w in words {}
    │              ──┬──
    │                ╰──── walked where it is
    │
    │ Help: declare it with `var`
    │
    │ Note: each pass calls `next()`, which changes the iterator; a variable is walked where it is, so after a `break` it is where the loop left it
────╯
